# A delayed triggered ability is controlled by the player who controlled the ability that created it (CR 603.7d-e), whoever
# controls its source afterwards. On turn 13 Bot1's Palace Jailer makes Bot1 the monarch and exiles Bot2's Dragon's Rage
# Channeler "until an opponent becomes the monarch" - an opponent of Bot1, whose ability that is. Bot2, holding Dack Fayden's
# emblem since turn 12, casts Restoration Magic's Cure on the Jailer and the emblem gives Bot2 the Jailer (checked). On
# turn 14 Bot2's Ragavan deals combat damage to Bot1, the monarch, so Bot2, Bot1's opponent, becomes the monarch, and the
# Channeler returns to the battlefield.

